  "result": "I've added `click.KeyValue`. It turns `--set a=b` into `(\"a\", \"b\")`, and the full test suite passes (1920 passed, 102 skipped, 1 expected failure). Ruff checks are clean. I didn't run mypy because it isn't installed here.\n\n**How it behaves:**\n- It splits on the first `=`, so `a=b=c` becomes `(\"a\", \"b=c\")`.\n- An empty value is allowed: `a=` becomes `(\"a\", \"\")`.\n- Input with no `=` (like `ab`), with an empty key (like `=b`), or an empty string fails. The error reads, for example: `Error: Invalid value for '--set': 'ab' is not a valid key=value pair.` (exit code 2).\n- With `multiple=True`, you get a list of pairs, which `dict(...)` turns straight into a dictionary.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`src/click/types.py`**: the new `KeyValue` class, next to the UUID type.\n- **`src/click/__init__.py`**: exports it as `click.KeyValue`.\n- **Docs**: added it to `docs/api.md` and the built-in types list in `docs/parameter-types.md`.\n- **`CHANGES.md`**: version 8.5.0 has already been released, so I started a new \"Version 8.6.0 \u2014 Unreleased\" section for this entry. The docstring is marked as added in 8.6 to match.\n- **Tests**:\n  - `tests/test_types.py`: direct checks of valid and invalid inputs.\n  - `tests/test_basic.py`: command-line tests, including the error message and `multiple=True`.\n  - `tests/test_info_dict.py`: a new entry for the type.\n\nRunning the formatter also reformatted `tests/test_defaults.py`, which isn't part of this change, so I undid that.\n\nNothing is committed yet.",
